import AFTD.Prelude
import AFTD.Kb.Tcs.SimpleGraphIsHop

/-!
# simple_graph_is_hop_closed

Topic: graphs   Node: 6850b7942e5c

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2610.18463 Question 5.9: The group generated by a graph's derangements

An edge subset F of a finite simple graph G is hop-closed (hop-maximal) if F is a subset of the edge set of G and for every edge e in E(G) \ F, the spanning subgraph with edges F ∪ {e} has strictly more hops than the spanning subgraph with edges F.
-/

/-- An edge subset of a finite simple graph is hop-closed (hop-maximal) if adding any edge strictly increases its number of hops. -/
def simple_graph_is_hop_closed {V : Type*} [Fintype V] (G : SimpleGraph V) (F : Set (Sym2 V)) : Prop :=
  F ⊆ G.edgeSet ∧
  ∀ e ∈ G.edgeSet \ F,
    Nat.card {h : Equiv.Perm V // simple_graph_is_hop (SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet F) h} <
    Nat.card {h : Equiv.Perm V // simple_graph_is_hop (SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet (insert e F)) h}
